1
00:00:08,225 --> 00:00:10,535
Last time, Basil touched this plant.

2
00:00:10,755 --> 00:00:12,035
And it folded up!

3
00:00:12,089 --> 00:00:13,119
I think it's shy.

4
00:00:13,279 --> 00:00:14,589
It's hiding from me!

5
00:00:15,019 --> 00:00:15,939
Is it shy?

6
00:00:16,149 --> 00:00:17,659
Did you lock in your answer?

7
00:00:17,899 --> 00:00:19,079
Hold on to it.

8
00:00:19,587 --> 00:00:21,107
Today is a field trip.

9
00:00:21,327 --> 00:00:22,817
Three stamps to collect.

10
00:00:23,247 --> 00:00:24,807
It's You against the Buddies.

11
00:00:25,027 --> 00:00:26,307
You lock in first.

12
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:28,257
One finger for every point.

13
00:00:28,477 --> 00:00:30,007
And a lizard is hiding.

14
00:00:30,237 --> 00:00:31,067
Find it!

15
00:00:32,392 --> 00:00:33,352
Round Zero.

16
00:00:33,572 --> 00:00:35,142
A rematch from last time!

17
00:00:35,372 --> 00:00:36,772
A plant does not eat.

18
00:00:37,002 --> 00:00:38,552
So how does it get its food?

19
00:00:38,792 --> 00:00:40,012
One, we feed it.

20
00:00:40,232 --> 00:00:41,732
Two, it makes its own.

21
00:00:41,982 --> 00:00:43,642
Three, it needs no food.

22
00:00:43,872 --> 00:00:45,282
Show me with your fingers.

23
00:00:50,754 --> 00:00:51,704
Locked in!

24
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:52,714
Two!

25
00:00:52,992 --> 00:00:56,132
Plants do not eat but they can make their own food when

26
00:00:55,882 --> 00:00:56,802
there is light.

27
00:00:56,936 --> 00:00:57,926
Two fingers?

28
00:00:58,156 --> 00:00:59,316
One finger up!

29
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:04,960
Are you ready?

30
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:06,140
Three!

31
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:07,170
Two!

32
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:08,170
One!

33
00:01:08,570 --> 00:01:09,240
Go!

34
00:01:10,623 --> 00:01:11,493
Round one.

35
00:01:11,743 --> 00:01:14,183
Basil touched one leaf, with one finger.

36
00:01:14,443 --> 00:01:15,253
Gently.

37
00:01:15,473 --> 00:01:16,543
It folded up.

38
00:01:16,783 --> 00:01:18,083
What happens next?

39
00:01:18,303 --> 00:01:19,833
One, it stays folded.

40
00:01:20,053 --> 00:01:21,603
Two, it opens again.

41
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:23,443
Three, the leaf drops off.

42
00:01:23,663 --> 00:01:25,073
Show me with your fingers.

43
00:01:30,549 --> 00:01:31,499
Locked in!

44
00:01:31,629 --> 00:01:32,199
One!

45
00:01:32,359 --> 00:01:33,219
It's shy.

46
00:01:33,299 --> 00:01:34,619
It will hide all day!

47
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:35,450
Two.

48
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:36,900
Nothing is torn.

49
00:01:36,946 --> 00:01:37,696
Two.

50
00:01:37,996 --> 00:01:39,766
All its other leaves are open.

51
00:01:40,262 --> 00:01:41,662
Let's wait and watch.

52
00:01:41,902 --> 00:01:43,102
From very close.

53
00:01:43,322 --> 00:01:44,302
Shrink down.

54
00:01:44,522 --> 00:01:45,402
Quietly.

55
00:01:48,187 --> 00:01:49,437
You are tiny now.

56
00:01:49,797 --> 00:01:51,717
You are standing on one of its leaves.

57
00:01:52,541 --> 00:01:53,931
One gentle touch.

58
00:01:55,455 --> 00:01:57,415
The little leaves fold inwards.

59
00:01:57,745 --> 00:01:58,805
Two by two.

60
00:02:00,317 --> 00:02:01,917
Then the whole leaf droops.

61
00:02:03,436 --> 00:02:04,596
Now, we wait.

62
00:02:07,506 --> 00:02:10,096
A few minutes later, the leaves open again.

63
00:02:12,619 --> 00:02:13,899
The answer is two.

64
00:02:14,129 --> 00:02:15,599
The leaves opened again.

65
00:02:15,738 --> 00:02:18,738
The mimosa plant is commonly called touch-me-not.

66
00:02:20,996 --> 00:02:22,386
The touch was a change.

67
00:02:22,596 --> 00:02:24,666
The mimosa folded its leaves.

68
00:02:24,876 --> 00:02:25,976
It responded.

69
00:02:26,697 --> 00:02:27,807
Say it with me!

70
00:02:28,517 --> 00:02:31,887
Living things respond to changes in the environment.

71
00:02:35,846 --> 00:02:39,566
The mimosa plant folds its leaves to protect itself from harm.

72
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:40,550
Not shy.

73
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:41,670
Responding!

74
00:02:42,878 --> 00:02:43,868
Two fingers?

75
00:02:44,098 --> 00:02:45,258
One finger up!

76
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:47,122
You respond too.

77
00:02:47,352 --> 00:02:50,102
In bright sunlight, your eyelids shut at once.

78
00:02:50,322 --> 00:02:51,722
That protects your eyes.

79
00:02:52,454 --> 00:02:53,654
Say it with me!

80
00:02:54,366 --> 00:02:58,686
The ability to respond to changes in our environment helps to protect

81
00:02:58,436 --> 00:03:00,926
us from danger and keeps us safe.

82
00:03:03,122 --> 00:03:07,032
Plants are also able to respond to changes in the environment.

83
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:10,420
Our plant on the window ledge grows towards the sunlight.

84
00:03:12,256 --> 00:03:13,216
My list.

85
00:03:13,446 --> 00:03:15,616
Three things that responded today.

86
00:03:15,826 --> 00:03:17,656
A snail pulled into its shell.

87
00:03:17,826 --> 00:03:19,486
An ice cream melted.

88
00:03:19,686 --> 00:03:21,196
A door banged shut.

89
00:03:21,547 --> 00:03:23,017
Something is not right.

90
00:03:23,227 --> 00:03:25,327
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

91
00:03:25,547 --> 00:03:26,457
Hold on!

92
00:03:31,964 --> 00:03:33,074
Arms crossed?

93
00:03:33,294 --> 00:03:34,434
One finger up!

94
00:03:34,634 --> 00:03:36,424
The sun melted the ice cream.

95
00:03:36,634 --> 00:03:38,094
The wind pushed the door.

96
00:03:38,324 --> 00:03:39,914
They are non-living things.

97
00:03:40,134 --> 00:03:41,144
They changed.

98
00:03:41,354 --> 00:03:42,924
But they did not respond.

99
00:03:43,424 --> 00:03:45,084
The snail is a living thing.

100
00:03:45,314 --> 00:03:49,014
Momo touched it, and it pulled into its shell to protect itself.

101
00:03:49,244 --> 00:03:50,564
That is responding.

102
00:03:50,623 --> 00:03:53,553
So not everything that changes is responding!

103
00:03:54,128 --> 00:03:55,038
Your turn.

104
00:03:55,258 --> 00:03:57,338
Find a mimosa on a grass patch.

105
00:03:57,558 --> 00:03:59,178
One finger, one leaf.

106
00:03:59,378 --> 00:04:01,218
The stem has tiny prickles.

107
00:04:01,428 --> 00:04:02,818
Never pull the plant.

108
00:04:03,038 --> 00:04:04,328
And wash your hands.

109
00:04:04,918 --> 00:04:06,308
Show me your score hand!

110
00:04:06,538 --> 00:04:07,548
More than two?

111
00:04:07,778 --> 00:04:09,058
You beat the Buddies.

112
00:04:09,278 --> 00:04:10,338
Three fingers?

113
00:04:10,558 --> 00:04:11,558
High five!

114
00:04:12,355 --> 00:04:13,715
Did you spot the lizard?

115
00:04:13,965 --> 00:04:15,505
It was on the garden sign.

116
00:04:15,735 --> 00:04:18,135
A lizard runs away when you come close.

117
00:04:18,365 --> 00:04:19,675
Is that responding?

118
00:04:19,875 --> 00:04:21,165
Tell someone at home.

119
00:04:21,963 --> 00:04:24,123
Let's read today's key words together!

120
00:04:24,363 --> 00:04:25,083
Ready?

121
00:04:25,373 --> 00:04:26,213
Mimosa.

122
00:04:27,686 --> 00:04:29,246
Respond to changes.

123
00:04:31,234 --> 00:04:32,134
Well done!

124
00:04:33,182 --> 00:04:35,512
Next stop: a farm in Kranji.

125
00:04:35,722 --> 00:04:38,992
This hen has kept five eggs warm for twenty-one days.

126
00:04:39,212 --> 00:04:40,582
Will every egg hatch?

127
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:42,302
Find out in Part Two!

128
00:04:44,059 --> 00:04:45,115
Say it with us!

129
00:04:45,915 --> 00:04:46,625
Ready?

130
00:04:46,749 --> 00:04:47,369
One!

131
00:04:47,749 --> 00:04:48,429
two!

132
00:04:48,754 --> 00:04:49,929
Now you know!
